// ─── SEED EXTENSION 2026-07-11 — third pillar: operational immunity ─────────
// Source: seven_ideas_deep.vsm ideas 1, 5, 6 (DS, 2026-07-05) as corrected by
// claude_review_seven_ideas.vsm §4. P5 already has two anti-capture pillars:
// anti_capture_by_design (the MOTOR cannot be repurposed) and governed_agency
// (the machine cannot sign the ENDS). This extension adds the third:
// operational immunity (the RECORD cannot be silently rewritten) — plus the
// identity metric that makes capture measurable.

operational_immunity: {
  claim:
    "The Merkle-chained, Ed25519-signed event log plus its verifier ecology
     (diverse_verifier, S3*, A0 classifier, algedonic channel) constitutes an
     immune layer: it distinguishes self (valid signature + intact chain)
     from non-self (foreign writer, broken chain, forged event) and responds
     with escalation. For anti-corruption this is the load-bearing property:
     corruption REQUIRES rewriting or suppressing the record; an immune
     record makes the attempt itself the detectable event.",

  framing_lock:
    "Claim ORGANIZATIONAL CLOSURE, not full autopoiesis — the kernel binary
     does not produce itself, and Git also has Merkle chains. Precedent for
     applying autopoietic categories to non-biological systems: Luhmann
     (social systems). The defensible statement: the event loop is
     organizationally closed (events → state → decisions → events, no path
     around the chain) and partially self-producing once learned modes ship.",

  measurables:
    "immune_response_time (injection → detection; gated by verifier cadence —
     expect a step at the next poll, NOT a biological response curve),
     false_positive_rate (restart_seam vs genuine — task AC-M3-FPR),
     self_tolerance (restart_seam accepted without alarm). The blind-injection
     challenge is already tasked (AUTOIMMUNE-TEST). These three numbers turn
     'tamper-evident' from a design adjective into a measured property —
     exactly what an anti-corruption deployment must certify to a regulator.",
}

decision_irreversibility: {
  claim:
    "Signed decisions are append-only and non-repudiable: |D(t)| is monotone.
     This irreversibility is the accountability substrate — an institution
     whose decisions cannot be un-made can be audited; one whose decisions
     can be silently reversed cannot. (No entropy 'second law' is claimed for
     the ledger — the empirical decision-type distribution may concentrate;
     only the count is monotone.)",

  capture_observable:
    "d|D|/dt as institutional metabolic rate: baseline in homeostasis, spikes
     under stress. For anti-corruption: a captured unit's decision rate and
     decision-type mix shift BEFORE individual decisions look anomalous —
     the same leading-indicator logic as the Lyapunov drift claim, at the
     governance layer. Baseline measurement tasked (AC-M4-DECISION-RATE).",
}

identity_metric_d_id: {
  claim:
    "D_id = the set of state dimensions persistently at the viability
     boundary ∂Ω. These are the constraints that BIND — the system's
     load-bearing identity. A change in D_id means the system is no longer
     the same system, whatever its code and branding say. For capture
     detection this is the deepest observable: capture is precisely a change
     in which constraints bind (whose interests the system optimizes), and
     D_id measures that directly.",

  covenant_link:
    "S5's covenant DEFINES the intended D_id; the measured D_id certifies it.
     Divergence between covenant-declared and measured binding constraints =
     capture in progress. This closes the loop with governed_agency: the
     covenant says what the identity should be, the offline S5 key makes
     changing it a human act, and D_id measurement detects drift between
     the declared and the actual.",

  caveat:
    "D_id must be validated as regime-stable first (idle vs loaded) — a dim
     near ∂Ω under one load pattern is not yet identity. Formalization
     tasked from OMEGA-MARGIN-DIAG data (review §4.idea_6).",
}
